  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of stationary wave is :\n$y=2 a \\sin \\left(\\frac{2 \\pi n t}{\\lambda}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{2 \\pi x}{\\lambda}\\right) \\text {. }$\nWhich of the following is NOT correct :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ed7Du",
      "text": "The dimensions of $n / \\lambda$ is [T]",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AWHqO",
      "text": "The dimensions of $\\mathrm{n}$ is $\\left[\\mathrm{LT}^{-1}\\right]$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "t6Lks",
      "text": "The dimensions of $x$ is [L]",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "86YbQ",
      "text": "The dimensions of $\\mathrm{nt}$ is [L]",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Comparing the given equation with standard equation of standing $\\frac{2 \\pi n}{\\lambda}=\\omega \\& \\frac{2 \\pi}{\\lambda}=k$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& {\\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{n}}{\\lambda}\\right]=[\\omega]=\\mathrm{T}^{-1}} \\\\\n& {[\\mathrm{nt}]=[\\lambda]=\\mathrm{L}} \\\\\n& {[\\mathrm{n}]=[\\lambda \\omega]=\\mathrm{LT}^{-1}} \\\\\n& {[\\mathrm{x}]=[\\lambda]=\\mathrm{L}}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
